WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.510
Her father died when she was young.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:52.570
Her mother lives and works in a Chinese restaurant.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:58.580
At the age of thirteen, Maya Kitajima faced many hardships.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.780
Maya Kitajima.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:08.540
Who discovered the fire that burned in this young girl's heart?

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:14.870
Episode 1 - The Girl with a Thousand Masks

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:20.870
Chinatown

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:25.870
I'm home!

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.020
You're late! You're so late!

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.610
What took you so long?

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.460
Sorry!

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.870
I told you to come home as soon as school was over!

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.900
It's all right, Miss Haru.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.880
I've got some deliveries for you, Maya.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:46.850
Okay!

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.600
Three bowls of ramen...

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.490
These are going to the Nanboku Hippodrome, right?

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.470
Nanboku, my foot!

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.790
I'm off then!

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.660
The Hippodrome...?

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.890
You...

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.350
Thanks for the delivery!

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:29.230
No, thank you!

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:33.520
And tomorrow, we'll be in Shimoda. I'm so happy.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.990
Will you take me with you?

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:37.990
Yes.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.090
So that's Oshima...

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.060
Yes.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.230
I mean, just look at how huge it is.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.090
Please drop by.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:51.850
When I arrive in Shimoda, I'll ask my mother to buy me a new hairbrush...

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.600
and then, I'll join you.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.250
There will be so much to do!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.550
I can't wait until tomorrow.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:03.030
Whereabouts in Tokyo do you live?

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:05.790
The Dancing Girl of Izu

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.750
10,000 Luck

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.000
It took you an hour and a half to make a simple delivery!

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.600
What a useless girl!

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.010
I apologize!

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.980
She won't hear the end of this!

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:25.750
Maya, you don't care, do you?! You're just making fun of me!

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:44.470
It doesn't matter what you say to this girl! She doesn't listen!

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.270
Sugiko! Turn that TV off already!

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:53.050
I guess she just can't resist, even when she's working.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:55.900
Maya really does like movies.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.200
She doesn't care about singing contests or quiz shows,

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.400
but you might as well talk to the wall when she's watching a drama.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.100
Ouch!

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.200
Did you prick your finger again?

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.680
What a clumsy girl!

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.750
You can't even sew a button on properly!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.630
Jeez... you're such a good-for-nothing.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.430
Just like your late father.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.010
I'm starting to lose patience with my own child!

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.070
Are you trying to sneak a peak again?

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.360
I hate it when you do that.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.620
The Snow Festival

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.260
There's a new movie out!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.350
I wonder who's starring in it...

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:14.400
I guess it's Utako Himekawa.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.520
It looks good!

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:23.270
If I...  it won't hurt to stay for a little while...

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.980
The noodles have gone all soggy!

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.220
Wandering off in the middle of a delivery to watch a movie!

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:44.470
And what am I supposed to tell the customer?

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.000
I'm very sorry! It won't happen again!

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.720
How can you do this to me?

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:52.600
A girl like you is never going to make anything of her life!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:55.100
You cause me nothing but embarrassment!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.930
Get out of my sight!

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.180
Well, well... this'll blow over like always.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:08.560
But why do you like TV programs and movies so much?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:13.910
I don't know... but as soon as I see the screen,

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.140
it's like I forget everything else!

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.480
Everything?

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:22.310
Yes! When I'm watching something, I feel like I become one of the characters...

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.410
and I lose myself.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:28.110
I feel like I'm an on-screen heroine.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:31.760
Unlike my normal, useless self.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.180
And that's when the head honcho appeared.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:47.990
And he said: "Now, look here... who do you think you're talking to?!"

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:49.850
And then what happened?!

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:52.030
Then, a gutsy woman arrived and said:

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:57.250
"And what are you meant to be? A man or a pig?"

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:05.270
"I get it. You're Don Porky."

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:11.720
"What did you call me?!"

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:20.910
What's your name?

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:22.140
Huh?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:26.530
I've searched everywhere and spent years looking for someone like you!

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.520
Yes, you'd be perfect.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:32.310
A girl like you would be perfect for the part...

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:34.600
Tell me - where do you live?

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.320
Please let go of me!

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:44.240
Wait!

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:46.010
Stop right there!

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.260
I've finally found her.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:58.010
Unless my eyes deceived me, she's the girl...

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.970
with a thousand masks!

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:40.390
They say the pork pies are really good there!

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:45.020
I really want to go see that.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:48.840
I've never seen a live performance before.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:51.820
I wonder what <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i> will be like...

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.560
I want to go so badly!

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.100
Not that I could ever afford tickets like those.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:59.400
As it happens, I've got a ticket for it!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.090
Sugiko!

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.550
You're jealous, aren't you?

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.840
It's a present from my boyfriend.

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:10.120
Sugiko... that ticket...

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:12.070
You want it?

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.360
This isn't a joke!

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:24.290
This happens to be the busiest time of the year!

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:31.950
End of Year Special!

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:31.950
Still Accepting Reservations

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:31.950
10,000 Luck Restaurant

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.420
You can't just skip work!

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.420
Mom, what's wrong?

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.140
One of our part-timers quit.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.020
Really?

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:39.970
How are we supposed to get tonight's deliveries done with only these two around?

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:44.900
Maya, you can have this ticket.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:46.160
You mean it?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:51.370
But only if you deliver all the End of Year Specials by yourself!

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:54.370
All of them... by myself?!

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.500
And they must be delivered on the thirty-first of December!

00:10:58.870 --> 00:10:59.700
Huh?

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:07.000
Which means you have to get them done before the ship in Yokohama Bay sounds its horn at midnight.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.930
All right, I'll do it.

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:13.600
I'll do every single one of those deliveries!

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.970
Don't be ridiculous!

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:19.330
There's no way you can deliver ninety-nine orders by yourself!

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:23.440
I'll get it done!

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.060
So, can I have the ticket to see <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i> ?

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:43.050
I'm from 10,000 Luck - here's your ramen!

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:45.540
I see you're nice and early again!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.310
I told them it'd be fine to deliver them at ten tonight.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.010
We're not ready to eat yet, but that's okay...

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:15.750
Delivery for six!

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:49.530
Here you go!

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:08.110
Hey, Maya! Are you doing all the deliveries by yourself tonight?

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:44.700
If there's even a <i>single</i> order left when the ship sounds its horn,

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:48.380
I'm keeping the ticket for <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i> !

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:26.230
I'm from 10,000 Luck! Here's your End of Year Soba!

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:34.140
Happy New Year!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.380
Happy New Year!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.550
I can't believe it.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:13.920
Looks like she managed to deliver the last order on the stroke of midnight.

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:14.850
She did?

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.480
How's that even possible?!

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:20.800
I guess that means she managed all ninety-nine orders!

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.370
But how?

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:27.300
I wonder what made her push herself so hard?

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:40.820
Sugiko, I did it. I delivered all of them by midnight!

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:43.890
Maya...

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:49.390
So, can I have that ticket to see <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i> ? You promised!

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:53.300
But you're supposed to go to that show with me!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.490
Fine... take it!

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:58.010
What does this ticket even matter to me anyway?!

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.470
Have it!

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.330
The ticket!

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:27.310
It's not my fault! The wind took it!

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.150
Why don't you just give up on it?

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.520
A performance like <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i> is too good for you anyway.

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:45.540
Hey!

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:54.090
Maya?!

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:12.290
Maya,

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:15.110
what are you doing?

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:18.140
You're going to get yourself killed!

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.320
Maya!

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:31.940
I've got it! I've got it!

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:35.650
It's mine... the ticket is mine!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.690
Now I'll get to see the show...

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.520
What the hell is wrong with this girl?

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:46.040
This ticket means I can see <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i> .

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.320
Did she fall into the bay?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:56.860
How can someone get so worked up over a theater ticket?

00:17:57.580 --> 00:18:02.000
What kind of life is this girl going to lead?

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:03.920
What can you see from Heaven, my dear husband?

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:50.950
La Dame aux Camelias

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.770
Excuse me!

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:04.530
Are you all right?

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:05.510
Yes...

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:07.330
Are you looking for your seat?

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:10.800
Yes... it's J35.

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:16.520
Please show this young lady to seat J35.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:21.270
As you wish, Mr. Hayami.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.440
Mr. Hayami?

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:44.510
Look! It's Utako Himekawa's husband: the director, Mitsugo Himekawa.

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:46.930
And that's their daughter, Ayumi Himekawa.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:51.550
Ayumi is only thirteen years old, but she's been acting since she was five.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:52.440
That's right.

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:56.970
They say she's extremely talented and will become an even better actress...

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:58.630
than her mother.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.020
Wow, she's so pretty!

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:05.130
So that's Utako Himekawa's daughter.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:11.030
She's thirteen, huh? I can't believe we're the same age.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:13.580
Then I'll let you enjoy the show, little one.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:14.900
"Little one?!"

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.540
Oh, Mr. Hayami!

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:20.420
So, that man's named Hayami?

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:21.530
Yes.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.940
He's going to become the next director of this theater,

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:28.030
as well as the director of all the cinemas and theaters in this city.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:33.920
He's been supporting rising stars from all over the country.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:35.420
Wow...

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:41.310
Alman... We have come so far together,

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:45.760
living in such happiness... And now...

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:50.270
Please let this happiness continue until we die!

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:06.500
If you see a white camellia... you'll know that we are meant to be together!

00:21:18.530 --> 00:21:22.020
A red camellia means that all is lost!

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:28.310
This is our sign... the sign of our secret love!

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:33.740
At the time, nobody could know that these two thirteen year old girls, Ayumi Himekawa...

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:42.270
and Maya Kitajima, would become bitter rivals,

00:21:42.590 --> 00:21:47.520
on a path drenched with blood and tears.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:24.740 --> 00:23:30.110
Maya Kitajima, a girl who memorized every line word-for-word...

00:23:30.110 --> 00:23:35.590
and all the subtle acting touches of the performers of a three-and-a-half hour performance

00:23:35.590 --> 00:23:40.300
of <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i> . And all this after only seeing it once.

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:44.270
You truly possess a thousand masks.

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:49.260
You are the only one who can fulfill my dreams.

00:23:46.620 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 2 - The Mask of Vivi
